@misc{jocher_ultralyticsyolov5_2022,
	title = {ultralytics/yolov5: v7.0 - {YOLOv5} {SOTA} {Realtime} {Instance} {Segmentation}},
	copyright = {Open Access},
	shorttitle = {ultralytics/yolov5},
	url = {https://zenodo.org/record/3908559},
	doi = {10.5281/ZENODO.3908559},
	abstract = {\&lt;div align="center"\&gt; \&lt;a align="center" href="https://ultralytics.com/yolov5" target="\_blank"\&gt; \&lt;img width="850" src="https://github.com/ultralytics/assets/blob/master/yolov5/v70/splash.png"\&gt;\&lt;/a\&gt; \&lt;/div\&gt; \&lt;br\&gt; Our new YOLOv5 v7.0 instance segmentation models are the fastest and most accurate in the world, beating all current SOTA benchmarks. We've made them super simple to train, validate and deploy. See full details in our Release Notes and visit our YOLOv5 Segmentation Colab Notebook for quickstart tutorials. \&lt;div align="center"\&gt; \&lt;a align="center" href="https://ultralytics.com/yolov5" target="\_blank"\&gt; \&lt;img width="800" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/26833433/203348073-9b85607b-03e2-48e1-a6ba-fe1c1c31749c.png"\&gt;\&lt;/a\&gt; \&lt;/div\&gt; \&lt;br\&gt; Our primary goal with this release is to introduce super simple YOLOv5 segmentation workflows just like our existing object detection models. The new v7.0 YOLOv5-seg models below are just a start, we will continue to improve these going forward together with our existing detection and classification models. We'd love your feedback and contributions on this effort! This release incorporates {\textless}strong{\textgreater}280 PRs{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} from {\textless}strong{\textgreater}41 contributors{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} since our last release in August 2022. Important Updates {\textless}strong{\textgreater}Segmentation Models ⭐ NEW{\textless}/strong{\textgreater}: SOTA YOLOv5-seg COCO-pretrained segmentation models are now available for the first time (https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9052 by @glenn-jocher, @AyushExel and @Laughing-q) {\textless}strong{\textgreater}Paddle Paddle Export{\textless}/strong{\textgreater}: Export any YOLOv5 model (cls, seg, det) to Paddle format with python export.py --include paddle (https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9459 by @glenn-jocher) {\textless}strong{\textgreater}YOLOv5 AutoCache{\textless}/strong{\textgreater}: Use {\textless}code{\textgreater}python train.py --cache ram{\textless}/code{\textgreater} will now scan available memory and compare against predicted dataset RAM usage. This reduces risk in caching and should help improve adoption of the dataset caching feature, which can significantly speed up training. (https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/10027 by @glenn-jocher) {\textless}strong{\textgreater}Comet Logging and Visualization Integration:{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} Free forever, Comet lets you save YOLOv5 models, resume training, and interactively visualise and debug predictions. (https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9232 by @DN6) New Segmentation Checkpoints We trained YOLOv5 segmentations models on COCO for 300 epochs at image size 640 using A100 GPUs. We exported all models to ONNX FP32 for CPU speed tests and to TensorRT FP16 for GPU speed tests. We ran all speed tests on Google Colab Pro notebooks for easy reproducibility. Model size\&lt;br\&gt;\&lt;sup\&gt;(pixels) mAP\&lt;sup\&gt;box\&lt;br\&gt;50-95 mAP\&lt;sup\&gt;mask\&lt;br\&gt;50-95 Train time\&lt;br\&gt;\&lt;sup\&gt;300 epochs\&lt;br\&gt;A100 (hours) Speed\&lt;br\&gt;\&lt;sup\&gt;ONNX CPU\&lt;br\&gt;(ms) Speed\&lt;br\&gt;\&lt;sup\&gt;TRT A100\&lt;br\&gt;(ms) params\&lt;br\&gt;\&lt;sup\&gt;(M) FLOPs\&lt;br\&gt;\&lt;sup\&gt;@640 (B) YOLOv5n-seg 640 27.6 23.4 80:17 {\textless}strong{\textgreater}62.7{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} {\textless}strong{\textgreater}1.2{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} {\textless}strong{\textgreater}2.0{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} {\textless}strong{\textgreater}7.1{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} YOLOv5s-seg 640 37.6 31.7 88:16 173.3 1.4 7.6 26.4 YOLOv5m-seg 640 45.0 37.1 108:36 427.0 2.2 22.0 70.8 YOLOv5l-seg 640 49.0 39.9 66:43 (2x) 857.4 2.9 47.9 147.7 YOLOv5x-seg 640 {\textless}strong{\textgreater}50.7{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} {\textless}strong{\textgreater}41.4{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} 62:56 (3x) 1579.2 4.5 88.8 265.7 All checkpoints are trained to 300 epochs with SGD optimizer with {\textless}code{\textgreater}lr0=0.01{\textless}/code{\textgreater} and {\textless}code{\textgreater}weight\_decay=5e-5{\textless}/code{\textgreater} at image size 640 and all default settings.\&lt;br\&gt;Runs logged to https://wandb.ai/glenn-jocher/YOLOv5\_v70\_official {\textless}strong{\textgreater}Accuracy{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} values are for single-model single-scale on COCO dataset.\&lt;br\&gt;Reproduce by {\textless}code{\textgreater}python segment/val.py --data coco.yaml --weights yolov5s-seg.pt{\textless}/code{\textgreater} {\textless}strong{\textgreater}Speed{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} averaged over 100 inference images using a Colab Pro A100 High-RAM instance. Values indicate inference speed only (NMS adds about 1ms per image). \&lt;br\&gt;Reproduce by {\textless}code{\textgreater}python segment/val.py --data coco.yaml --weights yolov5s-seg.pt --batch 1{\textless}/code{\textgreater} {\textless}strong{\textgreater}Export{\textless}/strong{\textgreater} to ONNX at FP32 and TensorRT at FP16 done with {\textless}code{\textgreater}export.py{\textless}/code{\textgreater}. \&lt;br\&gt;Reproduce by {\textless}code{\textgreater}python export.py --weights yolov5s-seg.pt --include engine --device 0 --half{\textless}/code{\textgreater} New Segmentation Usage Examples Train YOLOv5 segmentation training supports auto-download COCO128-seg segmentation dataset with {\textless}code{\textgreater}--data coco128-seg.yaml{\textless}/code{\textgreater} argument and manual download of COCO-segments dataset with {\textless}code{\textgreater}bash data/scripts/get\_coco.sh --train --val --segments{\textless}/code{\textgreater} and then {\textless}code{\textgreater}python train.py --data coco.yaml{\textless}/code{\textgreater}. {\textless}pre{\textgreater}{\textless}code class="lang-bash"{\textgreater}\# Single-GPU python segment/train.py --model yolov5s-seg.pt --data coco128-seg.yaml --epochs 5 --img 640 \# Multi-GPU DDP python -m torch.distributed.run --nproc\_per\_node 4 --master\_port 1 segment/train.py --model yolov5s-seg.pt --data coco128-seg.yaml --epochs 5 --img 640 --device 0,1,2,3 {\textless}/code{\textgreater}{\textless}/pre{\textgreater} Val Validate YOLOv5m-seg accuracy on ImageNet-1k dataset: {\textless}pre{\textgreater}{\textless}code class="lang-bash"{\textgreater}bash data/scripts/get\_coco.sh --val --segments \# download COCO val segments split (780MB, 5000 images) python segment/val.py --weights yolov5s-seg.pt --data coco.yaml --img 640 \# validate {\textless}/code{\textgreater}{\textless}/pre{\textgreater} Predict Use pretrained YOLOv5m-seg to predict bus.jpg: {\textless}pre{\textgreater}{\textless}code class="lang-bash"{\textgreater}python segment/predict.py --weights yolov5m-seg.pt --data data/images/bus.jpg {\textless}/code{\textgreater}{\textless}/pre{\textgreater} {\textless}pre{\textgreater}{\textless}code class="lang-python"{\textgreater}model = torch.hub.load('ultralytics/yolov5', 'custom', 'yolov5m-seg.pt') \# load from PyTorch Hub (WARNING: inference not yet supported) {\textless}/code{\textgreater}{\textless}/pre{\textgreater} Export Export YOLOv5s-seg model to ONNX and TensorRT: {\textless}pre{\textgreater}{\textless}code class="lang-bash"{\textgreater}python export.py --weights yolov5s-seg.pt --include onnx engine --img 640 --device 0 {\textless}/code{\textgreater}{\textless}/pre{\textgreater} Changelog Changes between {\textless}strong{\textgreater}previous release and this release{\textless}/strong{\textgreater}: https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/compare/v6.2...v7.0 Changes {\textless}strong{\textgreater}since this release{\textless}/strong{\textgreater}: https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/compare/v7.0...HEAD \&lt;details\&gt; \&lt;summary\&gt;🛠️ New Features and Bug Fixes (280)\&lt;/summary\&gt; * Improve classification comments by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/8997 * Update `attempt\_download(release='v6.2')` by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/8998 * Update README\_cn.md by @KieraMengru0907 in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9001 * Update dataset `names` from array to dictionary by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9000 * [segment]: Allow inference on dirs and videos by @AyushExel in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9003 * DockerHub tag update Usage example by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9005 * Add weight `decay` to argparser by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9006 * Add glob quotes to detect.py usage example by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9007 * Fix TorchScript JSON string key bug by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9015 * EMA FP32 assert classification bug fix by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9016 * Faster pre-processing for gray image input by @cher-liang in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9009 * Improved `Profile()` inference timing by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9024 * `torch.empty()` for speed improvements by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9025 * Remove unused `time\_sync` import by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9026 * Add PyTorch Hub classification CI checks by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9027 * Attach transforms to model by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9028 * Default --data `imagenette160` training (fastest) by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9033 * VOC `names` dictionary fix by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9034 * Update train.py `import val as validate` by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/pull/9037 * AutoBatch protect from negative